@try-works/dsh-browser-agent README · Install：Prerequisites: a DSH deployment with a profile (the **Web** surface is needed
for the pane; the tools work on any surface).

```powershell

@try-works/dsh-browser-agent README · Local development：```powershell
dsh plugin --profile web add link:D:/path/to/dsh-browser-agent
```

@try-works/dsh-browser-agent README · How it works：One package, two halves, both mounted from a single composition row:

**Host half (Node process)** — runs the browser, the tools, the skill, and the
pane server:

@try-works/dsh-browser-agent README · Work Mode：Credential-isolated web automation at ChatGPT Work parity. When enabled
(`workMode.enabled: true`), four layers keep credentials and consequential
actions out of the model's hands:

@try-works/dsh-browser-agent README · The model's tools：- `work_login_begin` / `work_login_cancel` / `work_login_status` — drive and
  inspect the supervised-login flow (never the credentials).
- `work_vault_status` — list sealed sessions (origins + cookie names only).

@try-works/dsh-browser-agent README · Publishing：```powershell
dsh plugin --profile web add @try-works/dsh-browser-agent
```

